    "double_toggle": "♠ ♠",
    "help_slate_use_title": "Slate and corrections",
    "help_slate_use_body": "The sheet and slate share the same rounds. On the slate, tap black space for points, a name to rename, ↶ to correct and × to close. The Z shows 100 at the top, 50 diagonally and 20 at the bottom; the remainder is in digits. Tap the Slate heading to show or hide round numbers. On the sheet, edit a field; clearing it also deletes later rounds. Each team’s ↶ arrow reopens its latest entry: announcements or round points. It does not step back through every earlier entry. For announcements, adjust quantities and confirm with OK: only that team changes. For round points, change the number and confirm: the opponents’ score is recalculated on the same row (157 minus your number, or 0 for a match of 257). The new value replaces the old one without adding a round. Cancel keeps the existing values. After a round, both teams’ arrows edit that same round from their own side; controls face the same way as their team’s Z.",
    "help_slate_ann_title": "Melds on the slate",
    "help_slate_ann_body": "The M button opens melds: 20 for 3 cards, 50 for 4 cards, 100 for 5 cards or four of a kind, 150 for four nines and 200 for four jacks. The 9 and J cards are illustrated in colour. Choose quantities with − and +, then press OK to apply the total once. Cancel changes nothing. Melds go only to the chosen team, with no complement to 157 for the opponent. The button is A in French, Italian and Romansh, and W in German. At 950 points, you can confirm 70 meld points: you reach 1020 and win. No new melds can be added after victory. On the slate, melds count before the round score: if confirming with OK reaches or exceeds 1000 in normal mode or 1500 in double spades mode, the winner is announced immediately, without waiting for a round. When the back arrow reopens a meld, the window is titled “Edit meld?”. Per team and round, you can enter at most 6 announcements of 20, 4 of 50 and 3 of 100. The + button is disabled at the limit, including when reopening the menu. Counters reset after the round. A match fills one round with 257 for one team and 0 for the other; another match belongs to the next round. Each team can use at most 18 cards for announcements per round: 20 uses 3 cards, 50 uses 4, 100 uses 5, and 150 and 200 each use 4. Previously confirmed announcements are included. The shared 100 row for five cards or four of a kind is counted as 5 cards.",
    "help_slate_read_title": "Reading and correcting the slate",
    "help_slate_read_body": "Top strokes are worth 100, diagonal strokes 50 and bottom strokes 20; the remainder is written as digits. Each group of five consists of four strokes crossed by a diagonal fifth stroke. Melds of 50 stay on the 50 line and scores of 20 on the 20 line, even when their sum reaches 100. A meld of 150 gives one 100 stroke and one 50 stroke. The white ↶ arrow below the 20 line reopens that team’s last entry with its value filled in; score entries also show the round number. Update replaces the entry, adjusts the opponent’s points if needed and does not create a new round. Older entries without saved details may not be editable. If correcting the last round reaches or exceeds 1000 points, or 1500 in double spades mode, the winner panel appears again even if it was previously closed. This applies to both the score sheet and the slate.",
    "help_slate_double_title": "Double spades and ending a game",
    "help_slate_double_body": "The central “♠ ♠ ON/OFF” button applies to both teams. OFF uses a 1000-point target; ON uses 1500 and doubles scores and melds. Always enter single scores: 100 versus 57 becomes 200 versus 114, a 257 match is worth 514 and a meld of 50 is worth 100. Switching modes also recalculates totals already entered. The first team to reach or exceed the target wins; the message appears above the slate. New game asks for confirmation, saves the game in history and resets the points. History shows saved games labelled Slate game. Back to the game returns to the slate.",
    "round_numbers": "Round number",
    "close_victory": "Close the victory panel",
    "help_round_options_title": "Showing round numbers",
    "help_round_options_body": "On the slate, tap its title to open the “Round number ON/OFF” menu. ON shows the numbers and OFF hides them. OK applies and remembers your choice and closes the menu; Cancel closes it without changes. After each confirmed round, its number appears in a column to the right of each team, below the name and total, spread over that half of the slate. The latest number is underlined. Melds and corrections do not create a new round.",
